From 999b1319a443b9109ad4fdec5d3ff8735ec36ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:29:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: honour dynamic colour write masks; add
 ms_input_fetch

Dynamic colour write masks and colour write enables were ignored: blending
is lowered in the shader with the pipeline's static masks, and Metal
pipelines always wrote every channel. Pipelines with dynamic masks now
get Metal pipeline variants with matching writeMask values, built on
first use and selected at draw time. Half-Life: Alyx relies on this for
a luminance draw that must not write colour.

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=ms_input_fetch lowers multisampled colour input
attachment reads to framebuffer fetches in shaders other than custom
resolve shaders. Metal then runs those shaders per sample, each reading
its own sample. A by-region barrier deferred in the final segment of a
custom-resolve pass no longer splits the pass for a draw whose fragment
shader reads no multisampled texture. The fragment shader key now
includes the ms_input_fetch and tile_resolve flags.

Debugging aids: KK_DUMP_RESOLVE_DIR (with KK_DUMP_RESOLVE_FIRST, _STEP
and _COUNT) writes the custom resolve output of selected passes to
files, and KK_SEQ_MSL_DIR saves the MSL of fragment shaders drawn in
KK_SEQ_LOG passes, along with their colour, depth and stencil state.

